WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
An AI agent that books trains and pays for them, under financial-services controls.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.000
Left: the requester asks for a trip (real timetable, simulated fares).

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:17.900
LLM proposes, code disposes: the model types the request, code does the rest.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:24.300
Quote ready. The requester cannot approve their own spend: the four-eyes rule.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.800
Right: the approver signs in. The waiting quote is announced, never opened for them.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.200
The approver reviews trains and quote hash, and lets the agent pay from the wallet.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.600
Approved: a single-use token for exactly this amount, merchant and run.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.900
Booked and confirmed by the processor, with the receipt and the quote hash.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.600
Seconds later the requester's window follows the decision on its own.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.000
Every step lands in a hash-chained audit trail, verified here.
